spans.s:
1 विध् विध॑ति (˚ते) serve a god (dat.);
 worship,
honour with (instr.);
 offer, consecrate (acc.);
 be gracious or friendly
(of a god). — उप worship, do homage.

2 विध् विन्ध॑ते lack, be destitute of (instr.);
 be bereft
or alone.

विधा॑न n. disposing, arranging (also adj., f. ई);
performing, accomplishing, creating, creation (also concr.);
 ordering,
ordinance, rule prescription, method;
 fate, destiny.

विधर्तृ॑ m. distributer, arranger, maintainer,
supporter;
 loc. as inf. to distribute or to hold.

1 वि॑धर्मन् m. holder, supporter, arranger;
 enclosure,
receptacle, limits;
 arrangement, disposition, direction.

विधा॑ f. part, proportion, measure, sort, kind;
 adj. —˚
often -fold, -like.

विधातृ॑ m. disposer, distributer, arranger, creator, N.
of a god, often identif. with Brahman or a son of Brahman;
 also Fate
personified, E. of Viṣṇu, Śiva etc.;
 f. विधात्री disposing,
arranging, creating.

विधायक a. & m. regulating, ordering;
 builder,
founder, author.

विधा˚यिन् a. & m. regulating, ordering;
 builder, founder,
author.

विधि m. disposition, arrangement, ordinance, prescription,
rule, method, way, procedure, means of (dat., loc., or —˚);
 act, the
action of (—˚), performance, business, work;
 solemn act, ceremony;
creation, fate, destiny;
 the Creator or Brahman.

विधुर m. robbed of the pole (carriage);
 i.g. bereft,
alone;
 separated from, destitute of, lacking (—˚);
 defective,
incomplete;
 depressed, wretched, miserable;
 adverse, contrary,
unfavourable;
 n. adv., as subst. adversity, misfortune.

विधूनन a. causing to move hither and thither;
 n.
shaking, agitating;
 waving, undulating;
 rejecting, removing.

वि॑धृत a. kept asunder, separated, distributed;
 shunned,
avoided;
 kept back, detained, preserved;
 held, borne, worn, possessed,
taken (resolution).

विधेय a. to be granted, procured, used, employed;
 to be
(being) ordered or enjoined;
 to be established or stated;
 to be
performed or done, shown or manifested;
 subject or obedient to,
dependent on (gen. or —˚). n. what is to be done, incumbency, duty.

विध्वस्त a. raised (dust);
 decayed, perished,
destroyed, lost.
